            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Koegaki 1.2.1</h2>
<ul>
    <li>When you change your settings, Koegaki now keeps the previous copy as a backup. If the saved copy is ever damaged, Koegaki goes back to that backup instead of resetting to defaults.</li>
    <li>From this version on, Koegaki remembers your launch at login choice and turns it back on if an update switches it off.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
